+# CONTRACT — Reactive Spreadsheet Engine
+
+Definition of done. Every criterion has a test in `src/*.test.ts`.
+
+## Cell reference parsing
+- [ ] Parse `A1` -> col 0, row 0 (0-based internal) -> test
+- [ ] Parse multi-letter columns `AA1`, `AZ1`, `BA1`, `Z100` -> test
+- [ ] Column letter <-> index round-trips (A=0, Z=25, AA=26, AZ=51, BA=52) -> test
+- [ ] Invalid references throw (`1A`, `A`, `A0`, `AB`, ``, `A-1`) -> test
+
+## Raw value storage & retrieval
+- [ ] set/get number -> `get` returns number -> test
+- [ ] set/get string -> `get` returns string -> test
+- [ ] set/get boolean -> `get` returns boolean -> test
+- [ ] get empty cell returns `null` -> test
+- [ ] getDisplay of empty cell returns `""` -> test
+- [ ] getDisplay number/string/boolean returns string form ("42", "hello", "true") -> test
+
+## Formula arithmetic
+- [ ] `=1+2` -> 3; `=10-4` -> 6; `=3*4` -> 12; `=12/4` -> 3 -> test
+- [ ] operator precedence `=2+3*4` -> 14 -> test
+- [ ] parentheses `=(2+3)*4` -> 20 -> test
+- [ ] unary minus `=-5`, `=-A1`, `=3+-2` -> test
+- [ ] division by zero throws / yields error -> test
+- [ ] decimals `=3.14*2` -> 6.28 -> test
+
+## Cell references in formulas
+- [ ] `=A1` returns A1's value -> test
+- [ ] `=A1+B1` adds two cells -> test
+- [ ] reference to empty cell treated as 0 in arithmetic -> test
+- [ ] reference to string/boolean cell in arithmetic: boolean true=1/false=0; non-numeric string -> error -> test
+
+## Built-in functions
+- [ ] SUM over column/row/block range -> test
+- [ ] AVERAGE -> mean of numeric values -> test
+- [ ] MIN / MAX -> test
+- [ ] COUNT -> count of numeric cells (ignores empty/string/bool) -> test
+- [ ] functions ignore empty & non-numeric cells in range -> test
+- [ ] AVERAGE of no numeric values -> 0 (or error) — define: returns 0 -> test
+- [ ] functions accept scalar args too e.g. `=SUM(A1, A2, 5)` -> test
+- [ ] nested function calls `=SUM(A1:A3)+MAX(B1:B3)` -> test
+
+## IF and comparisons
+- [ ] `=IF(A1>30,"big","small")` -> test
+- [ ] comparison operators >, <, >=, <=, =, <> -> test
+- [ ] IF only evaluates chosen branch (lazy) -> test (branch with error not taken still works)
+- [ ] string equality comparison `=IF(A1="x",1,0)` -> test
+
+## Ranges
+- [ ] column range A1:A5 expands to 5 cells -> test
+- [ ] row range A1:C1 expands to 3 cells -> test
+- [ ] block range A1:C3 expands to 9 cells -> test
+- [ ] reversed range B2:A1 normalized -> test
+
+## Reactive updates
+- [ ] changing A1 updates dependent B1=`=A1+1` -> test
+- [ ] transitive: A1 -> B1 -> C1 all update -> test
+- [ ] updating a cell to non-formula clears its dependencies -> test
+- [ ] range-dependent cell updates when any cell in range changes -> test (SUM)
+- [ ] dependents recompute when a referenced cell goes from empty to set -> test
+
+## Circular reference detection
+- [ ] direct cycle A1=`=B1`, B1=`=A1` throws -> test
+- [ ] indirect cycle A1->B1->C1->A1 throws -> test
+- [ ] self reference A1=`=A1` throws -> test
+- [ ] cycle through a range (A1=`=SUM(A1:A3)`) throws -> test
+- [ ] after a throw, spreadsheet state remains consistent (old value kept) -> test
+
+## getCells
+- [ ] returns Map of all non-empty cells to computed values -> test
+- [ ] excludes empty cells -> test
+
+## Example from spec
+- [ ] full example usage scenario passes -> test
